Subject: Attention Frame Response Mode Operational Faults

@ [fault_ledger_uuid] 68a36087-f0c9-4ab4-8fe2-93570554bbbf

& [AFRM_F001] is first compact projection below its declared reduction target
  + [observed] full was 3052 bytes and first compact was 1188 bytes or 2.569-to-one
  + [cause] run and manifest identities were duplicated in AttentionFrame RETURN and an exterior proof_ref wrapper
  + [containment] verification semantics remained correct and the result was not accepted as meeting AFRM-005
  + [repair] canonical specification identifies RETURN as the minimal evidence reference and removes only redundant wrapper data
  + [proof] successor compact result is 1005 bytes or 3.0368-to-one with exact evidence fields retained
  + [status] is closed

& [AFRM_F002] is strict-mode access to an intentionally absent compact property
  + [observed] first reproducibility-script run accessed frame.runtime directly and PowerShell rejected the absent property
  + [containment] the check failed before claiming a measurement result and Codex configuration remained unchanged
  + [repair] absence is inspected through the object's declared property-name collection under unchanged strict mode
  + [proof] successor three-family run passes and invalid ratio plus injection-shaped host parameters refuse before readiness work
  + [status] is closed

& [AFRM_F003] is an SSH remote-process audit command with broken nested PowerShell quoting
  + [observed] the verified negative MCP probe completed first but two subsequent inline process-count attempts were parsed by the remote command shell instead of PowerShell
  + [containment] both attempts were read-only and made no process service configuration or file change
  + [repair] encode the fixed remote PowerShell script as UTF-16LE Base64 and invoke powershell.exe with -EncodedCommand
  + [proof] repaired audit reports zero cantor-attention-mcp processes after the ephemeral probe
  + [status] is closed

& [AFRM_F004] is a final audit lookup against a guessed local deployed-config name
  + [observed] deployment manifest hashing succeeded but experiments/needle2_attention_mcp/config.json does not exist
  + [cause] the repository preserves the reviewed operator config as config.evox2.example.json while deployment names the selected copy config.json
  + [containment] the lookup was read-only and its missing value was not accepted as proof
  + [repair] resolve the repository path from inventory and independently hash the exact remote selected path
  + [proof] repository example remote selected config and deployment-manifest claim all equal 818a43df51b8bbfe4a7d8abe38458efbe4ad9c946dc0504d78f28e09f9ebf45c
  + [status] is closed

& [AFRM_F005] is malformed local construction of an encoded temporal-audit script
  + [observed] the first command string failed local PowerShell parsing before SSH invocation
  + [containment] no remote command ran and no state changed
  + [repair] use a literal here-string before UTF-16LE Base64 encoding
  + [proof] three samples over forty seconds each report llama PID 12780 and zero persistent cantor-attention-mcp processes
  + [status] is closed
